1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,313
A pack of cars screams past the

2
00:00:03,313 --> 00:00:04,760
grandstand.

3
00:00:05,090 --> 00:00:07,705
Every surface you can see has been

4
00:00:07,705 --> 00:00:08,281
sold:

5
00:00:08,281 --> 00:00:09,039
the boards,

6
00:00:09,039 --> 00:00:09,798
the cars,

7
00:00:09,798 --> 00:00:11,079
the overalls,

8
00:00:11,079 --> 00:00:13,510
even the time on the screen.

9
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:15,783
The race on track is only half

10
00:00:15,783 --> 00:00:17,232
the story.

11
00:00:17,483 --> 00:00:18,187
Last year,

12
00:00:18,187 --> 00:00:20,858
the company that runs Formula One took

13
00:00:20,858 --> 00:00:23,432
in 3.9 billion dollars,

14
00:00:23,432 --> 00:00:26,752
14 percent more than the year before.

15
00:00:27,017 --> 00:00:30,587
So where does that money come from?

16
00:00:30,707 --> 00:00:31,434
Who pays,

17
00:00:31,434 --> 00:00:32,412
who gets paid,

18
00:00:32,412 --> 00:00:34,419
and why do cities line up to

19
00:00:34,419 --> 00:00:36,175
host a race that can cost them

20
00:00:36,175 --> 00:00:37,527
a fortune?

21
00:00:37,627 --> 00:00:40,720
This is The Hidden Economics.

22
00:00:46,383 --> 00:00:47,464
At its core,

23
00:00:47,464 --> 00:00:50,003
Formula One is simple.

24
00:00:50,083 --> 00:00:52,808
A handful of teams design their own

25
00:00:52,808 --> 00:00:53,383
cars,

26
00:00:53,383 --> 00:00:56,103
and race them around the world.

27
00:00:56,423 --> 00:00:57,976
For most of its history,

28
00:00:57,976 --> 00:00:59,953
that was the whole idea.

29
00:01:00,183 --> 00:01:02,801
The business began when someone realised

30
00:01:02,801 --> 00:01:04,982
the show itself could be packaged and

31
00:01:04,982 --> 00:01:05,800
sold.

32
00:01:06,050 --> 00:01:07,293
For decades,

33
00:01:07,293 --> 00:01:09,551
that someone was Bernie Ecclestone,

34
00:01:09,551 --> 00:01:12,089
who sold the sport to television as

35
00:01:12,089 --> 00:01:13,450
one package.

36
00:01:13,670 --> 00:01:15,564
In 2006,

37
00:01:15,564 --> 00:01:18,074
the investment firm CVC took majority

38
00:01:18,074 --> 00:01:19,130
control.

39
00:01:19,150 --> 00:01:20,611
According to CVC,

40
00:01:20,611 --> 00:01:22,839
the calendar grew from sixteen to

41
00:01:22,839 --> 00:01:26,163
twenty-two races while it was in charge.

42
00:01:26,417 --> 00:01:28,131
In 2016,

43
00:01:28,131 --> 00:01:31,229
the American media company Liberty Media

44
00:01:31,229 --> 00:01:33,067
agreed to buy Formula One,

45
00:01:33,067 --> 00:01:35,854
valuing the business at 8 billion dollars,

46
00:01:35,854 --> 00:01:37,487
including its debt.

47
00:01:37,607 --> 00:01:40,741
The deal closed in January 2017,

48
00:01:40,741 --> 00:01:42,775
and a new era began.

49
00:01:48,417 --> 00:01:51,397
Today the sport has three layers.

50
00:01:51,397 --> 00:01:54,407
The FIA writes and polices the rules.

51
00:01:54,407 --> 00:01:55,473
Formula One,

52
00:01:55,473 --> 00:01:57,411
owned by Liberty Media,

53
00:01:57,411 --> 00:01:59,369
holds the commercial rights and sells the

54
00:01:59,369 --> 00:02:00,187
show.

55
00:02:00,247 --> 00:02:01,462
And the teams compete,

56
00:02:01,462 --> 00:02:03,297
sharing in the money.

57
00:02:03,327 --> 00:02:05,807
Liberty's own filings say the FIA must

58
00:02:05,807 --> 00:02:08,536
put safety and sporting concerns above

59
00:02:08,536 --> 00:02:11,864
Formula One's commercial interests.

60
00:02:12,117 --> 00:02:14,307
Liberty has kept building.

61
00:02:14,307 --> 00:02:16,012
In 2025,

62
00:02:16,012 --> 00:02:17,839
it also bought most of MotoGP,

63
00:02:17,839 --> 00:02:19,877
the motorbike championship.

64
00:02:20,037 --> 00:02:21,323
Two world series,

65
00:02:21,323 --> 00:02:22,710
one owner.

66
00:02:28,350 --> 00:02:30,440
Here is the business model,

67
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:31,980
in one drawing.

68
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:34,480
In the middle sits Formula One.

69
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:36,719
Money flows in from broadcasters,

70
00:02:36,719 --> 00:02:38,204
from race promoters,

71
00:02:38,204 --> 00:02:39,810
and from sponsors.

72
00:02:39,810 --> 00:02:41,706
And a large share flows back out

73
00:02:41,706 --> 00:02:42,491
again,

74
00:02:42,491 --> 00:02:43,904
to the teams.

75
00:02:44,150 --> 00:02:44,918
Last year,

76
00:02:44,918 --> 00:02:47,885
media rights brought in 31 percent of

77
00:02:47,885 --> 00:02:49,280
the revenue.

78
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:50,745
Race promotion fees,

79
00:02:50,745 --> 00:02:52,910
about 27 percent.

80
00:02:52,910 --> 00:02:53,799
Sponsorship,

81
00:02:53,799 --> 00:02:56,040
about 22 percent.

82
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:58,758
The rest came from hospitality,

83
00:02:58,758 --> 00:03:00,639
freight and licensing.

84
00:03:00,883 --> 00:03:02,990
And the total keeps climbing,

85
00:03:02,990 --> 00:03:04,297
year after year,

86
00:03:04,297 --> 00:03:09,404
to 3.9 billion dollars across 24 races.

87
00:03:15,050 --> 00:03:17,750
Media rights are the biggest single

88
00:03:17,750 --> 00:03:18,650
stream.

89
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,229
By our calculation,

90
00:03:20,229 --> 00:03:23,066
they were worth about 1.2 billion dollars

91
00:03:23,066 --> 00:03:24,080
last year.

92
00:03:24,450 --> 00:03:27,666
Broadcasters pay to show every session,

93
00:03:27,666 --> 00:03:30,368
and Formula One also sells its own

94
00:03:30,368 --> 00:03:33,400
streaming service directly to fans.

95
00:03:33,650 --> 00:03:36,960
The biggest new deal is in America.

96
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:39,400
Apple is now the sport's exclusive

97
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:42,137
broadcaster in the United States,

98
00:03:42,137 --> 00:03:43,490
for five years.

99
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:45,568
The price was never disclosed,

100
00:03:45,568 --> 00:03:48,849
but it is reportedly about 140 million

101
00:03:48,849 --> 00:03:50,280
dollars a year.

102
00:03:50,517 --> 00:03:52,497
Why pay that much?

103
00:03:52,557 --> 00:03:54,657
Look at the American audience.

104
00:03:54,687 --> 00:03:55,435
On ESPN,

105
00:03:55,435 --> 00:04:00,235
the average race drew 554,000 viewers in

106
00:04:00,235 --> 00:04:01,867
twenty eighteen.

107
00:04:02,117 --> 00:04:03,968
By twenty twenty-five,

108
00:04:03,968 --> 00:04:06,544
it was 1.3 million,

109
00:04:06,544 --> 00:04:09,237
up 135 percent.

110
00:04:14,883 --> 00:04:17,923
The second stream is the hosting fee.

111
00:04:18,083 --> 00:04:20,656
Circuits and cities pay Formula One for

112
00:04:20,656 --> 00:04:22,893
the right to stage a Grand Prix.

113
00:04:23,023 --> 00:04:25,607
Contracts typically run three to seven

114
00:04:25,607 --> 00:04:26,053
years,

115
00:04:26,053 --> 00:04:28,073
with fees rising by up to 5

116
00:04:28,073 --> 00:04:29,613
percent a year.

117
00:04:29,763 --> 00:04:31,432
By our calculation,

118
00:04:31,432 --> 00:04:33,755
those fees came to about 1 billion

119
00:04:33,755 --> 00:04:35,323
dollars last year.

120
00:04:35,583 --> 00:04:37,638
The fee for each race is almost

121
00:04:37,638 --> 00:04:39,523
never published.

122
00:04:39,543 --> 00:04:41,384
But we know who often pays:

123
00:04:41,384 --> 00:04:43,629
Liberty says some of its partners are

124
00:04:43,629 --> 00:04:44,903
governments.

125
00:04:45,063 --> 00:04:46,026
In Singapore,

126
00:04:46,026 --> 00:04:48,937
the twenty twenty-two race cost about 100

127
00:04:48,937 --> 00:04:50,293
million dollars to stage,

128
00:04:50,293 --> 00:04:53,086
and the government covered 60 percent of

129
00:04:53,086 --> 00:04:53,882
it.

130
00:04:54,117 --> 00:04:56,687
Las Vegas is the exception.

131
00:04:56,687 --> 00:04:57,148
There,

132
00:04:57,148 --> 00:05:00,087
Formula One is its own promoter.

133
00:05:00,087 --> 00:05:01,896
It bought land beside the Strip for

134
00:05:01,896 --> 00:05:04,542
about 240 million dollars,

135
00:05:04,542 --> 00:05:05,877
built a pit building,

136
00:05:05,877 --> 00:05:08,365
and keeps the ticket and hospitality

137
00:05:08,365 --> 00:05:09,417
money.

138
00:05:09,517 --> 00:05:11,444
It takes the reward,

139
00:05:11,444 --> 00:05:12,881
and the risk.

140
00:05:18,517 --> 00:05:20,440
Sponsorship is the third stream,

141
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:22,193
and it is growing fast:

142
00:05:22,193 --> 00:05:25,382
about 22 percent of revenue last year,

143
00:05:25,382 --> 00:05:27,087
up from less than a fifth the

144
00:05:27,087 --> 00:05:28,417
year before.

145
00:05:28,787 --> 00:05:31,695
The luxury group LVMH signed a ten-year

146
00:05:31,695 --> 00:05:33,617
global partnership.

147
00:05:33,707 --> 00:05:36,234
The oil giant Aramco joined earlier,

148
00:05:36,234 --> 00:05:39,015
with Formula One promising it an audience

149
00:05:39,015 --> 00:05:41,655
of 500 million fans.

150
00:05:41,917 --> 00:05:44,217
Then there is hospitality.

151
00:05:44,217 --> 00:05:45,575
In the Paddock Club,

152
00:05:45,575 --> 00:05:47,877
corporate guests watch from above the pit

153
00:05:47,877 --> 00:05:48,607
lane.

154
00:05:48,607 --> 00:05:50,026
Hospitality,

155
00:05:50,026 --> 00:05:52,432
freight and licensing together brought in

156
00:05:52,432 --> 00:05:55,870
another 787 million dollars.

157
00:06:01,517 --> 00:06:04,167
So how do the teams get paid?

158
00:06:04,187 --> 00:06:04,640
First,

159
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:07,527
a share of Formula One's profits.

160
00:06:07,527 --> 00:06:08,176
Last year,

161
00:06:08,176 --> 00:06:11,242
Formula One paid the teams 1.4 billion

162
00:06:11,242 --> 00:06:11,891
dollars,

163
00:06:11,891 --> 00:06:15,068
about 60 percent of its underlying profit

164
00:06:15,068 --> 00:06:16,767
before those payments.

165
00:06:16,767 --> 00:06:19,939
And that sum has grown every year.

166
00:06:20,183 --> 00:06:20,864
Second,

167
00:06:20,864 --> 00:06:22,085
their own sponsors:

168
00:06:22,085 --> 00:06:23,705
the logos on the car,

169
00:06:23,705 --> 00:06:26,183
the overalls and the garage.

170
00:06:26,263 --> 00:06:27,018
Mercedes,

171
00:06:27,018 --> 00:06:27,966
for example,

172
00:06:27,966 --> 00:06:30,829
reported revenue of about 810 million

173
00:06:30,829 --> 00:06:32,551
dollars in twenty twenty-four,

174
00:06:32,551 --> 00:06:34,525
with more than 60 percent of it

175
00:06:34,525 --> 00:06:36,673
from sponsorship and licensing.

176
00:06:36,863 --> 00:06:40,341
Its profit was about 150 million dollars.

177
00:06:40,583 --> 00:06:44,473
So keep three pots of money apart.

178
00:06:44,523 --> 00:06:46,763
Formula One's own revenue.

179
00:06:46,763 --> 00:06:48,323
The teams' revenue.

180
00:06:48,323 --> 00:06:49,807
And the promoters,

181
00:06:49,807 --> 00:06:51,819
who pay the hosting fee and sell

182
00:06:51,819 --> 00:06:53,173
the tickets.

183
00:06:58,817 --> 00:06:59,620
For years,

184
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:02,113
the richest teams could simply outspend

185
00:07:02,113 --> 00:07:03,217
the rest.

186
00:07:03,217 --> 00:07:04,972
So in twenty twenty-one,

187
00:07:04,972 --> 00:07:07,057
the sport brought in a cost cap:

188
00:07:07,057 --> 00:07:10,286
145 million dollars that first year,

189
00:07:10,286 --> 00:07:13,887
falling to 135 million dollars.

190
00:07:14,047 --> 00:07:15,683
From twenty twenty-six,

191
00:07:15,683 --> 00:07:18,930
it rises to 215 million dollars,

192
00:07:18,930 --> 00:07:21,427
but it now covers far more costs.

193
00:07:21,537 --> 00:07:23,925
Driver salaries and the three best-paid

194
00:07:23,925 --> 00:07:26,913
executives are still outside it.

195
00:07:27,150 --> 00:07:28,600
And the cap has teeth.

196
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:31,342
Red Bull Racing went over its twenty

197
00:07:31,342 --> 00:07:35,150
twenty-one limit by 1.6 percent.

198
00:07:35,190 --> 00:07:36,411
The penalty:

199
00:07:36,411 --> 00:07:37,467
a 7-million-dollar fine,

200
00:07:37,467 --> 00:07:41,400
and 10 percent less aerodynamic testing.

201
00:07:41,650 --> 00:07:44,272
With costs capped and income shared,

202
00:07:44,272 --> 00:07:47,185
teams have started to look like profitable

203
00:07:47,185 --> 00:07:48,580
franchises.

204
00:07:48,910 --> 00:07:52,118
Forbes estimates that the average team was

205
00:07:52,118 --> 00:07:55,226
worth 3.6 billion dollars last year,

206
00:07:55,226 --> 00:07:58,607
with Ferrari on top at 6.5 billion

207
00:07:58,607 --> 00:07:59,700
dollars.

208
00:07:59,950 --> 00:08:01,705
That is why a seat at the

209
00:08:01,705 --> 00:08:04,060
table is so expensive.

210
00:08:04,350 --> 00:08:07,119
When Cadillac was approved as an eleventh

211
00:08:07,119 --> 00:08:07,524
team,

212
00:08:07,524 --> 00:08:10,889
it reportedly agreed to pay 450 million

213
00:08:10,889 --> 00:08:12,359
dollars to the others,

214
00:08:12,359 --> 00:08:15,298
more than double the 200 million dollars

215
00:08:15,298 --> 00:08:16,555
in the old rules,

216
00:08:16,555 --> 00:08:18,259
to make up for sharing the prize

217
00:08:18,259 --> 00:08:20,137
money eleven ways.

218
00:08:25,783 --> 00:08:28,323
Why do brands pay so much?

219
00:08:28,373 --> 00:08:28,895
Reach,

220
00:08:28,895 --> 00:08:31,143
and a changing audience.

221
00:08:31,153 --> 00:08:34,720
Formula One says it had 827 million

222
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:35,728
fans last year,

223
00:08:35,728 --> 00:08:39,223
up 63 percent since twenty eighteen.

224
00:08:39,363 --> 00:08:42,329
And 42 percent of them are women.

225
00:08:42,583 --> 00:08:43,787
For a sponsor,

226
00:08:43,787 --> 00:08:46,491
that means a global stage almost every

227
00:08:46,491 --> 00:08:47,695
other weekend,

228
00:08:47,695 --> 00:08:49,145
a wealthy audience,

229
00:08:49,145 --> 00:08:52,083
and a technology story to tell.

230
00:08:52,083 --> 00:08:53,242
Aramco's deal,

231
00:08:53,242 --> 00:08:54,401
for example,

232
00:08:54,401 --> 00:08:57,365
also covered sustainable fuels.

233
00:09:03,017 --> 00:09:06,707
That audience did not grow by accident.

234
00:09:06,747 --> 00:09:09,081
In March 2019,

235
00:09:09,081 --> 00:09:11,566
Netflix released Drive to Survive,

236
00:09:11,566 --> 00:09:14,326
a behind-the-scenes series that turned

237
00:09:14,326 --> 00:09:17,687
drivers and team bosses into characters.

238
00:09:17,847 --> 00:09:20,343
The new owners pushed into social media

239
00:09:20,343 --> 00:09:21,567
and streaming.

240
00:09:21,637 --> 00:09:23,139
Then came Hollywood:

241
00:09:23,139 --> 00:09:24,812
a racing blockbuster,

242
00:09:24,812 --> 00:09:26,484
named after the sport,

243
00:09:26,484 --> 00:09:29,585
took more than 630 million dollars at

244
00:09:29,585 --> 00:09:31,155
the box office.

245
00:09:31,417 --> 00:09:33,927
And the calendar went global.

246
00:09:34,267 --> 00:09:35,903
Las Vegas joined,

247
00:09:35,903 --> 00:09:38,677
Madrid hosts the Spanish race from twenty

248
00:09:38,677 --> 00:09:39,758
twenty-six,

249
00:09:39,758 --> 00:09:42,531
and a ten-year deal will take Formula

250
00:09:42,531 --> 00:09:44,750
One to Rwanda in the early

251
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:46,459
twenty-thirties.

252
00:09:52,117 --> 00:09:53,880
For a host city,

253
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:55,971
a Grand Prix is a deal with

254
00:09:55,971 --> 00:09:57,467
two sides.

255
00:09:57,497 --> 00:09:58,435
On one side,

256
00:09:58,435 --> 00:09:59,853
a global audience,

257
00:09:59,853 --> 00:10:02,377
full hotels and a famous name.

258
00:10:02,477 --> 00:10:03,657
On the other,

259
00:10:03,657 --> 00:10:04,355
the fee,

260
00:10:04,355 --> 00:10:05,054
the track,

261
00:10:05,054 --> 00:10:07,099
and weeks of disruption.

262
00:10:07,350 --> 00:10:09,490
The bills can be large.

263
00:10:09,490 --> 00:10:11,994
The twenty twenty-four Australian Grand

264
00:10:11,994 --> 00:10:15,048
Prix cost Victorian taxpayers about 67

265
00:10:15,048 --> 00:10:16,210
million dollars.

266
00:10:16,210 --> 00:10:17,279
In Las Vegas,

267
00:10:17,279 --> 00:10:19,460
a study paid for by Formula One

268
00:10:19,460 --> 00:10:22,906
put the race's economic impact at 934

269
00:10:22,906 --> 00:10:23,974
million dollars,

270
00:10:23,974 --> 00:10:27,453
with 45 million dollars in direct taxes.

271
00:10:27,717 --> 00:10:30,177
Economists are sceptical.

272
00:10:30,307 --> 00:10:32,979
Independent studies of big sporting events

273
00:10:32,979 --> 00:10:35,873
nearly unanimously find that the promised

274
00:10:35,873 --> 00:10:38,477
benefits are exaggerated.

275
00:10:38,587 --> 00:10:41,406
Victoria's own Auditor-General found that

276
00:10:41,406 --> 00:10:43,262
for the twenty oh-five race,

277
00:10:43,262 --> 00:10:45,977
the costs exceeded the benefits.

278
00:10:46,067 --> 00:10:47,445
And in Las Vegas,

279
00:10:47,445 --> 00:10:50,459
local businesses complained of lost trade,

280
00:10:50,459 --> 00:10:53,628
until three of the disputes were settled.

281
00:10:59,283 --> 00:11:01,673
The risks are real.

282
00:11:01,803 --> 00:11:02,496
This spring,

283
00:11:02,496 --> 00:11:05,366
the Bahrain and Saudi Arabian races were

284
00:11:05,366 --> 00:11:07,757
called off because of the conflict in

285
00:11:07,757 --> 00:11:09,313
the Middle East.

286
00:11:09,613 --> 00:11:11,793
Fewer races means less money:

287
00:11:11,793 --> 00:11:13,665
in the first half of this year,

288
00:11:13,665 --> 00:11:17,393
Formula One's revenue fell 15 percent.

289
00:11:17,833 --> 00:11:19,814
Rights groups accuse some hosts of

290
00:11:19,814 --> 00:11:21,263
sportswashing.

291
00:11:21,263 --> 00:11:24,210
And sponsors cut back in a recession.

292
00:11:24,450 --> 00:11:27,580
But the opportunities are big too.

293
00:11:27,580 --> 00:11:29,800
A new American broadcaster.

294
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:31,410
An eleventh team.

295
00:11:31,410 --> 00:11:34,040
New markets in Spain and Africa.

296
00:11:34,220 --> 00:11:36,078
All the teams signed up to the

297
00:11:36,078 --> 00:11:39,000
sport's governance until twenty thirty.

298
00:11:39,130 --> 00:11:42,111
And new engines run on sustainable fuel,

299
00:11:42,111 --> 00:11:44,421
as Formula One aims for net zero

300
00:11:44,421 --> 00:11:47,193
carbon by 2030.

301
00:11:47,450 --> 00:11:50,470
Formula One sells speed.

302
00:11:50,570 --> 00:11:53,538
But the real product is attention:

303
00:11:53,538 --> 00:11:55,837
hundreds of millions of fans,

304
00:11:55,837 --> 00:11:57,554
